    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 271 of 2006",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S3799\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend chapter 271 of the laws of 2006, amending the\nenvironmental conservation law relating to adding areas of Ulster\ncounty within the Catskill park to the Hudson river valley greenway,\nin relation to the effectiveness of such chapter\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nRevives Chapter 271 of the Laws of 2006, relating to adding areas of\nUlster County within the Catskill Park to the Hudson River Valley\nGreenway and makes it permanent.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nAmends Section 3 of Chapter 271 of the Laws of 2006 amending the\nenvironmental conservation law relating to adding areas of Ulster\nCounty within the Catskill Park to the Hudson River Valley Greenway by\nremoving the expiration date, reviving the provisions of the law and\ndeeming them in full force and effect as they existed on December 31,\n2008.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\nUlster County communities located in the Catskill Park are no longer\neligible for membership in the Greenway since Chapter 271 of the Laws\nof 2006 expired on January 1, 2009.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nHudson River Valley Greenway has been a successful program that\nassists membership communities with natural and cultural resource\nprotection, regional planning, economic development, public access and\nheritage environmental education. Chapter 271 of the Laws of 2006\ngranted Ulster County communities located in the Catskill Park the\noption of joining the Greenway. This act expired on January 1, 2009.\nThis bill revives Chapter 271 of the Laws of 2006 and removes the\nexpiration, allowing those communities the continued opportunity for\nmembership in the Greenway.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n2008 - A.11168 - Vetoed by Governor\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall be deemed to have\nbeen in full force and effect on and after December 31, 2008.\n",
